ices and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 5.0 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 8.6, with a 95% confidence interval of 5.1 to 14.7. December accounts for 0% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 6% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 6. Contract [1], for 14,870 euros, was awarded in July 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts near the legal limit does not prove improper actions. It could reflect market conditions, budget constraints, or genuine needs. Statistical patterns alone do not indicate wrongdoing without further investigation.\nWhat can be checked: Check the contracts' details to confirm if they align with the body's needs. Review awardee A's contracts to see if they repeat the same services or goods. Examine if multiple contracts cover the same purpose to identify potential overlaps or inconsistencies.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["AuXiRIgSOGg36J9Lctlsuw%3D%3D","YdzBUN30WR1%2BF6L2uCfUWg%3D%3D","fGXJOOgZOa310HRJw8TEnQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}